# Mantaz Sectle

## Lore

Very insect-looking humanoids resembling a giant praying mantis, encased in natural mega-damage armor: bright green above, yellow, orange or tan beneath, with large yellow or gold eyes. Despite their looks they are warm-blooded, possibly related to birds, and neither eat nor enslave intelligent beings. Sectles keep to themselves in tiny communities of 1D6x10, both sexes superior hunters of animals. They fight only the dabugghs unprovoked; their looks make them targets of human supremacists and trigger-happy travelers. They make trustworthy and loyal friends, courageous in combat and gentle toward their own.

## GM Notes

Only the mantaz sectle of the several sectle types has been rifted to Earth, mainly to the British Isles decades ago, with tiny colonies in France and Africa. They prefer forests and jungles and love Millennium Trees, attacking only dabugghs or those who threaten the tree. A female lays 1D4 eggs each spring, secured in tall trees and watched day and night by 1D4 guardians. They number about half the dabugghs. Average NPC level 1D4+3.
', 'published', 'data-script'
